  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and clients pay for people who notice problems early. They judge you by accurate notes and calm reporting.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing ten facts about a place in two minutes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and develop observation skills: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools describe images and summarise notes. Routine description shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Noticing what matters, checking assumptions and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to organise notes and check them; later, own the judgments.
  </p>

